● Liberals also highlight the role of international law in reducing conflict. By establishing
norms and rules, legal frameworks reduce uncertainty and build trust between states.
○ Institutions such as the International Court of Justice and the World Trade
Organisation provide mechanisms for resolving disputes peacefully, further
reinforcing the liberal belief that global governance can help mitigate conflict.
The Impact and Growth of International Organisations
Liberals see international organisations as central to global politics.. These organisations provide
platforms for dialogue, foster economic and political collaboration, and promote collective action to
address global challenges.
● Liberal theorists argue that international organisations are a central part of global
governance in a deeply interconnected international system.
○ These institutions not only facilitate cooperation but also create norms and
standards that shape state behaviour.
● Realists argue that international organisations lack the power to enforce their decisions or
that states only comply with their rules when it serves their interests. However, liberals
counter that these organisations help build trust and stability over time, creating a
rules-based international order that benefits all participants and therefore means that states
comply with their rules and decisions the vast majority of the time.
